2027..2101 Comment "/// Reading twice is reading once at the same state. The inner `get` is an"
2102..2172 Comment "/// instance of the rule\'s own left side through its pattern, and both"
2173..2244 Comment "/// reducts read once and continue at that state three times (#2116). A"
2245..2396 Comment "/// scope over this theory runs its subject normalised by the rule: `let a = /// st.get(); let b = st.get(); pure a + b` reads once, `let a = st.get();"
2397..2470 Comment "/// pure a + a` with `b` bound to `a` (`state-laws.gandr`\'s `readTwice`)."
